<title>ITALY: Italy's Palermo sees Feb CPI at -0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Palermo sees Feb CPI at -0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO, Italy 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Palermo said its February consumer price index stood at -0.3 percent month on month and 1.4 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In January, Palermo's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 1.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Palermo is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.80 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.3   (0.1)     1.4  (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2   (0.0)     3.1  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	  -0.1   (0.0)     2.0  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -3.4   (0.3)    -3.0  (0.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.5   (0.0)     0.1  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2   (3.0)     3.5  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0  (-0.5)     2.1  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.6   (0.1)     1.3  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.4   (0.0)     3.4  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.4   (0.0)     1.6  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.0)    -0.9  (-0.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
